  "obligation_append": {
    "W-SSC-099": " The original ordered CP3 source map is rho_tw([z1,z2,z3,z4])=[-bar(z2),bar(z1),-bar(z4),bar(z3)]. W05 prints the HP1 affine quaternion chart q=(q2)^-1*q1 with inverse on the LEFT and maps CP3 to HP1 by pi([z1,z2,z3,z4])=[z1+z2j,z3+z4j], whose invariant CP1 fibers are not fixed individual projective points.",
    "W-SSC-101": " The source holomorphic fibration pi:R4×CP1→CP1 projects to the second factor and uses each base point to select an orthogonal complex structure on R4. The Pauli-matrix x1sigma1+x2sigma2+x3sigma3 has a SOURCE +1 eigenspace line O(1), not a -1 eigenline; two copies and then 2d copies are separately source stated.",
    "W-SSC-102": " W05 explicitly prints the hyperkähler family aI+bJ+cK with IJ=K and (a,b,c) on the unit sphere, then distinguishes invariance in one, two and three directions producing Bogomolny, Hitchin and Nahm/coadjoint-orbit cases respectively; these are cited source examples.",
    "W-SSC-104": " W05 explicitly gives M=H^1(X,GL(n,C)) as equivalence classes of pi1(X)-representations, a SET not a vector space, with no claimed higher-degree non-abelian cohomology; the distinct source parameter values lambda=1 usual connections and lambda=0 Higgs bundles are conserved.",
    "W-SSC-105": " W05's printed quaternion parameter laws ij=k, ji=-k, i²=a, j²=b require nonzero a,b in F. Hilbert symbol +1 means split M(2,F), while -1 means NOT split. The three quadratic extensions for p≠2 and equality of formerly different algebras only AFTER tensoring with K are separate source-scoped assertions.",
    "W-SSC-106": " W05's parameter conic -a*x²-b*y²+ab*z²=0 has F-points on Hilbert-sign +1 but NOT on -1. The finite-p conic -p*x²-u*y²+up*z²=0 has NO Qp points and HAS quadratic-extension K points on which the Z/2Z Galois action has no fixed points; the twistor comparison is an ANALOGY only.",
    "W-SSC-107": " W05 prints the Brauer equivalence A~B iff A⊗M_n(F) isomorphic B⊗M_m(F), the product [A][B]=[A⊗B], and an even/odd real Clifford complexification case: r+s=2n yields one M(2^n,C), r+s=2n+1 yields a DIRECT SUM of TWO copies. Preserve the branch indices, do not assert a qualified universal theorem.",
    "W-SSC-108": " W05's source [Q,P]=i1 uses hbar=1 on Schwartz S(R). For a quaternionic V the Weil carrier W_(a,b)=(F⊕F*)⊗(a,b/F) and Brauer Z/2Z class control local true/projective cases; Hilbert reciprocity product over ALL finite primes AND infinity equals 1 and the true adelic Weil representation is restricted to the diagonal Sp(W_(a,b),Q)."
  },
  "negative": [
